src/tree_packing/geometry/truncation.py::truncate_to_n. Grows a candidate
pool of both sublattices' points until it exceeds n, then keeps the n
closest to the origin by Chebyshev distance (the natural metric for a
square window). Validity is structural, not re-verified per call: any
subset of a feasible lattice (H3.1) stays overlap-free, since removing
trees cannot create new intersections.

Green: pytest tests/unit/test_truncation.py -- 2 passed, covering every n
in 21..200 plus determinism. Independently cross-checked a sample of five
