selection is implemented here; swap-move refinement is not. Produces a
valid truncation for every n (satisfying this sub-hypothesis), not
necessarily a tight one -- see the following H3.4 measurement, where this
shows up directly as boundary loss well above the milestone's own worked
example at every n tested.

